proof.text:
The naturality of the same term maps $t$ at $z_n:R_Y[0]\to P_n$, together with the tensor-unit normalization $\alpha_{E,R_Y}=1_{Rf_*E}$ from [lem-weil-pbc-ringed-projection-mate-exact], gives an equality of chain maps $\tau_n(1_N\otimes z_n)=f_*(1_I\otimes z'_n):N\to B_n$. These equalities commute with the transitions by the already established strict tower equation. Let $c_X(I)$ and $c_Y(N)$ denote the constant towers; the equalities assemble to the strict square
$$
\begin{CD}
c_Y(N) @>{\iota_Y}>> C_\bullet\\
@V{\cong}VV @VV{\tau_\bullet}V\\
f_*^{\operatorname{Tow}}c_X(I) @>{f_*^{\operatorname{Tow}}\iota_X}>> f_*^{\operatorname{Tow}}J_\bullet,
\end{CD}
$$
where $\iota_X$ and $\iota_Y$ are the maps induced by $1\otimes z'_\bullet$ and $1\otimes z_\bullet$.
